{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-gerbes}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:78ee3157bdfb168c194d5b8662dd788bce6b898ebf6595d5db220ab77abfa09f", "source_text": "Gerbes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ad03589971222caaec667a11a2d98b0fc882c6d6a28b8f7c68c0c6d63221cdf4", "unit_id": "tag:06QB:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$[B/G]$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$G$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{criteria-lemma-BG-algebraic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-local-structure-gerbe}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3cfd7d37590dc6f15c666d92af1f976c63485e7f3079ec48e3b2ca11f0af818d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6cdce0504648ce780c0f2c0163227d925665761911e6f5f733301f8cb9348ff4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAn important type of algebraic stack are the stacks of the\nform <MATH_0001> where <MATH_0002> is an algebraic space and <MATH_0003> is a flat\nand locally finitely presented group algebraic space over <MATH_0004>\n(acting trivially on <MATH_0005>), see\nCriteria for Representability, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIt turns out that an algebraic stack is a gerbe when it locally in the\nfppf topology is of this form, see\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nIn this section we briefly discuss this notion and the corresponding\nrelative notion.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f2afab16fa30618bf64472ef1f07395c000ed0ca4b6dbff574fd5ef01b75f83b", "unit_id": "tag:06QB:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-definition-gerbe-over-stack-in-groupoids}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-gerbe}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:21c217a8a61055d77def0ee5ae58b7be359cf84aabe701af1912b459c58c5983", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3d9cce00c011cec1117bfa8ff658ae80c409a31c1f5f443c3b3eff67f08791e9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>gerbe over<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0003> if\n<MATH_0004> is a gerbe over <MATH_0005> as stacks\nin groupoids over <MATH_0006>, see\nStacks, Definition <REF_0001>.\nWe say an algebraic stack <MATH_0007> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>gerbe<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if there exists\na morphism <MATH_0008> where <MATH_0009> is an algebraic space which\nturns <MATH_0010> into a gerbe over <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf74eec03b2fda5cfd604307f72dfd672e385e85fba80b719fe16405659fbba7", "unit_id": "tag:06QC:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-fppf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0eff82b643ea0b6a415fab5a7d95bebb3011f4eb78d1f97d23f00a468e049528", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:58aeb7dafedc35cf9a86e4e3f24385c7c183718814407e11749cedf9ce8c7f6a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe condition that <MATH_0001> be a gerbe over <MATH_0002> is defined\npurely in terms of the topology and category theory underlying the given\nalgebraic stacks; but as we will see later this condition has\ngeometric consequences. For example it implies that\n<MATH_0003> is surjective, flat, and\nlocally of finite presentation, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe absolute notion is trickier to parse, because it\nmay not be at first clear that <MATH_0004> is well determined. Actually, it is.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:de1b349b747d458caa688235a631ca17422563e99c1c07db4c3182e3e005ad7f", "unit_id": "tag:06QB:prose-0002"}
